# exclude.list — known, understood differences that the snapshot tools leave out of rows and
# digests by default. Both cpp_probe/snapshot.sh and verovio_dart/tool/snapshot.dart read this
# file (pass --sem-lista to see everything); the two dumps must be made with the same list or
# their digests are not comparable (snapshot_diff warns).
#
# One entry per line (text after # is a comment):
#   field          the field, for every class
#   class.field    the field, only for entities of that class label
#   key:<text>     every entity whose key contains <text>
#
# An entry hides state from the comparison, so every entry needs its reason here. A PORT
# DIVERGENCE (the Dart really differs from the C++) stays listed only while it is known not to
# reach the drawing — remove the entry when it is fixed or suspected.

# Class hierarchy: the Dart System extends SystemElement, a FloatingObject; the C++ System is a
# plain Object (system.h:36), so these FloatingObject fields exist only on the Dart side.
system.foCurrentPositioner
system.foGrpId
system.foMaxYRel

# PORT DIVERGENCE, found by the snapshot on 2026-09-11 (beam/beam-001.mei, from
# ScoreDefSetCurrentFunctor#1): the C++ keeps pgHead/pgFoot in a scoreDef of their own (they
# appear as a separate `scoreDef[1]` root), while the Dart copies them into every drawing
# scoreDef (page, system, measure). The keys can never pair up, so the entities are left out.
key:/pgHead[
key:/pgFoot[

# Dead state: the C++ writes Doc::m_drawingBeamMaxSlope (doc.cpp:2386, a float) and never reads
# it; the Dart field is never written (stays 0.0).
doc.dBeamMaxSlope
